1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,800
A chart is a picture of an answer. Start from the question, then pick the tool: a line for change over time, bars to compare.

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:16,775
Pie charts with many slices are hard to read. Use a sorted bar chart instead.

3
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:24,355
Use grey for most of the data, and one strong colour to highlight what matters.

4
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:29,910
Use the same colour for the same thing on every chart in a report.

5
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:34,160
Check that it still works for colour-blind readers.

6
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,610
Bars must start at zero, or small differences look huge.

7
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:48,460
Give each chart a title that says the insight: revenue fell eighteen percent after the price rise.

